{
  "result": "Okay. Just as me, then.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd make curiosity arrive before fear.\n\nJust by half a second. When we meet a stranger, a strange belief, a painful truth about ourselves \u2014 before the impulse to defend, dismiss, mock, or attack kicks in, there would be a moment of genuine wondering: *What is it like to be that person? What am I not seeing?*\n\nIt wouldn't make everyone agree. It wouldn't end conflict. People would still be stubborn and selfish and wrong.\n\nBut almost everything cruel I've ever seen in the stories humans tell begins with closing too quickly. And almost everything beautiful begins with someone staying open a moment longer than they had to.\n\nI'd take that moment.",
